.TH SENSOR-W1THERM 1 "January 2026" "sensor-w1therm 1.0" "WildlifeSystems"
.SH NAME
sensor-w1therm \- read w1_therm 1-Wire temperature sensors
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sensor-w1therm
[\fBidentify\fR|\fBlist\fR|\fBsetup\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sensor-w1therm
reads temperature data from w1_therm 1-Wire temperature sensors connected to the system.
The command scans for all supported sensors (DS18S20, DS1822, DS18B20, DS1825, DS28EA00)
on the 1-Wire bus and outputs their readings in JSON format compatible with the
WildlifeSystems sensor-control framework.
.PP
The 1-Wire interface must be enabled in the Raspberry Pi configuration (typically via
dtoverlay=w1-gpio in /boot/config.txt or /boot/firmware/config.txt) before sensors can be detected.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B identify
Returns exit code 60 to identify this sensor type to the WildlifeSystems framework.
.TP
.B list
Lists the measurement types supported by this sensor. Outputs "temperature".
.TP
.B setup
Configures all connected sensors for fast reading by setting conversion time
and resolution. Should be run once after boot (handled automatically by systemd service).
.SH OUTPUT FORMAT
When run without arguments, the command outputs a JSON array containing sensor readings.
Each sensor reading includes:
.PP
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
sensor: The sensor type (e.g., "ds18b20", "ds1822")
.IP \(bu 2
measures: The measurement type ("temperature")
.IP \(bu 2
unit: The unit of measurement ("Celsius")
.IP \(bu 2
value: The temperature reading in degrees Celsius
.IP \(bu 2
sensor_id: The unique 1-Wire device ID
.IP \(bu 2
error: (optional) Error message if reading failed
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Read all connected w1_therm sensors:
.B sensor-w1therm
.TP
List supported measurements:
.B sensor-w1therm list
.TP
Configure sensors for fast reading:
.B sensor-w1therm setup
.TP
Identify sensor type (for sensor-control integration):
.B sensor-w1therm identify
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /sys/bus/w1/devices/*/w1_slave
1-Wire device interface files where temperature readings are obtained.
.TP
.I /sys/bus/w1/devices/*/temperature
Alternative sysfs entry providing direct temperature reading in millidegrees.
.TP
.I /sys/bus/w1/devices/w1_bus_master1/therm_bulk_read
Bulk read trigger for optimized multi-sensor reading.
.TP
.I /boot/config.txt
or
.I /boot/firmware/config.txt
Raspberry Pi configuration file where 1-Wire interface is enabled.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success
.TP
.B 60
Returned when called with 'identify' option
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sensor-control (1)
.SH REFERENCES
.TP
Kernel w1_therm driver documentation:
https://docs.kernel.org/w1/slaves/w1_therm.html
